{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":29,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-ray]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","line":29,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Minimizing geodesics on an interval]\n\\label{def:minimizing-geodesic-window}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:minimizing-geodesic-ray}\n\n\n\n\n\nFor a metric space $(M,d)$ and $I\\subset\\Ar$, a map $\\gamma\\colon I\\to M$\nis a \\emph{unit-speed minimizing geodesic on $I$} if\n$$d(\\gamma(s),\\gamma(t))=|s-t|\\qquad(s,t\\in I).$$\nThe cases $I=[a,b]$, $[0,\\infty)$, and $\\Ar$ are called a minimizing\nsegment, ray, and line, respectively. Such maps are $1$-Lipschitz, and the\nproperty is preserved by restriction and translation of the parameter.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Minimizing geodesics on an interval] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6d696e696d697a696e672d67656f64657369632d77696e646f77\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">morgan-tian</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aminimizing-geodesic-ray\">↗ def:minimizing-geodesic-ray</a> <p></p>For a metric space <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,d)$\">$(M,d)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$I\\subset \\Ar $\">$I\\subset \\Ar $</span>, a map <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma \\colon I\\to M$\">$\\gamma \\colon I\\to M$</span> is a <em>unit-speed minimizing geodesic on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$I$\">$I$</span></em> if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ d(\\gamma (s),\\gamma (t))=|s-t|\\qquad (s,t\\in I). \\]\">\\[ d(\\gamma (s),\\gamma (t))=|s-t|\\qquad (s,t\\in I). \\]</span> The cases <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$I=[a,b]$\">$I=[a,b]$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[0,\\infty )$\">$[0,\\infty )$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Ar $\">$\\Ar $</span> are called a minimizing segment, ray, and line, respectively. Such maps are <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span>-Lipschitz, and the property is preserved by restriction and translation of the parameter. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-ray","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-ray","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-ray","label":"def:minimizing-geodesic-ray"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments","title":"def:has-min-segments","label":"def:has-min-segments"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing","title":"lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing","label":"lem:ultrafilter-limi